  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday Night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1136 AM CST Wed Nov 11 2026\n\nLong wave troughing will remain in place for the end of the week \nwith cold air settling into Middle TN. Highs on Friday will remain\nin the 40s after starting out in the 30s. Most of the precip will\ndiminish Thursday night but there is a low chance for a few \nlingering showers over the Plateau into Friday morning. There is \nsome uncertainty on how cool temperatures will get Thursday night \nbut we may see them get cold enough over the Plateau for some \nsnow to mix in with any of the showers. Not expecting any \naccumulation or impacts with snow but some areas could see their \nfirst snow flakes of the year. We will continue to see a low \nchance for scattered rain showers mainly over the Plateau for the\nafternoon and early evening. \n\nThe long wave trough will push east over the weekend and will \nbring dry weather but it will remain cold. Highs will be in the \n50s and lows in the 20s. Much of the area will see its first hard\nfreeze of the year Friday and Saturday night. Quiet weather\nremains in place into early next week as an upper level ridge \nbuilds over the Great Lakes with a strong surface high setting up\nto our north. Temperatures will gradually warm a bit every day \nand should reach the 60s again by mid-week. With a dry air mass in\nplace lows will remain chilly in the 20s and 30s.",
